        "procedure": "Hpyzha (60.8 mg, 0.4375 mmol) and Hpyzic (7.75 mg, 0.0625 mmol) were reacted with cobalt nitrate (145.5 mg, 0.5 mmol) and lanthanide nitrate (0.1 mmol) in MeOH (20 mL) to give a brown solution. Evaporation at room temperature for two months afforded dark brown crystals of {Co4IIILn8} (Ln = Dy3+ for 1).",
